{
  "conformance": "source.predicate",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "status": "ruled",
  "basis": [
    "SalesBlaster's segment predicates as its compiler evaluates them in DuckDB, with TRY_CAST for every typed read",
    "the predicate tree: filter, and, or and not, over dimension catalog 1.0.0"
  ],
  "rule": "Three-valued (Kleene) logic. A comparison over an absent key, a null value, or a value that does not convert to the dimension's type (TRY_CAST gives NULL) is unknown. not(unknown) is unknown. and: any false gives false, else any unknown gives unknown, else true. or: any true gives true, else any unknown gives unknown, else false. exists never gives unknown: exists=false is true exactly when the key is absent or null, exists=true is its negation. An unknown at the top is refused with reason unevaluable_value and never survives. An empty string never reaches the evaluator: admission maps it to absent.",
